on the left/right edges (x = 0 or x = W−1); in pairs 2 and 4 they sit on the top/bottom edges (y = 0 or y = H−1).\n\n**What the output does.** Each seed pixel becomes a full line running away from the edge it touches: seeds on the left/right edges become full rows, seeds on the top/bottom edges become full columns. Then the pair of lines is repeated as an alternating pattern. Taking the two line positions p1 < p2, the spacing is d = p2 − p1, and the output continues the lines at p2 + d, p2 + 2d, … with alternating colours (colour of p1, colour of p2, colour of p1, …) until the grid runs out:\n\n- Pair 1: rows 5 (colour 2) and 7 (colour 3), d = 2 → rows 9, 11, …, 21 alternate 2, 3, 2, … ✓\n- Pair 2: columns 5 (1) and 8 (3), d = 3 → columns 11, 14, 17, 20 ✓\n- Pair 3: rows 7 (4) and 11 (1), d = 4 → rows 15, 19, 23 ✓\n- Pair 4: columns 5 (2) and 7 (8), d = 2 → columns 9, 11, …, 23 ✓\n\nNothing is drawn before the first seed in any pair, so the pattern only extends in the increasing direction. This matches the fact sheet exactly (e.g. pair 3 adds 4-lines at 15 and 23 and a 1-line at 19).\n\n**Test input.** Seeds: colour 3 at (0,5) on the top edge and colour 4 at (10,10) on the bottom edge (H = 11), so the lines are vertical columns. Columns 5 (3) and 10 (4), d = 5, so further columns 15 (3), 20 (4), 25 (3); 30 is off the 27-wide grid.\n\n**Construction stages emitted:** first the two seed lines are drawn, then each repeated line is added one at a time.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    seeds = [(o[\"cells\"][0][0], o[\"cells\"][0][1], o[\"colour\"]) for o in objs]\n\n    # orientation: seeds on top/bottom edges -> vertical columns; on left/right edges -> horizontal rows\n    tb = sum(1 for y, x, c in seeds if y == 0 or y == H - 1)\n    lr = sum(1 for y, x, c in seeds if x == 0 or x == W - 1)\n    vertical = tb >= lr\n\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    def draw(pos, col):\n        if vertical:\n            out[:, pos] = col\n        else:\n            out[pos, :] = col\n\n    # positions along the perpendicular axis\n    lines = sorted(((x if vertical else y), c) for y, x, c in seeds)\n\n    # stage 1: extend each seed into a full line\n    for pos, col in lines:\n        draw(pos, col)\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Extend each seed pixel into a full line perpendicular to the edge it touches\")\n\n    if len(lines) >= 2:\n        p1, c1 = lines[0]\n        p2, c2 = lines[1]\n        d = p2 - p1\n        limit = W if vertical else H\n        cols = [c1, c2]\n        k = 2\n        pos = p2 + d\n        while d > 0 and pos < limit:\n            draw(pos, cols[k % 2])\n            emit(out.copy(), f\"Repeat the pattern: line at position {pos} with colour {cols[k % 2]} (spacing {d})\")\n            k += 1\n            pos += d\n\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Final alternating line pattern\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"repeat":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Then the pair of lines is repeated as an alternating pattern."},{"source":"final explanation","text":" p1 < p2, the spacing is d = p2 − p1, and the output continues the lines at p2 + d, p2 + 2d, … with alternating colours (colour of p1, colour of p2, colour of p1, …) until the grid runs out:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 1: rows 5 (colour 2) and 7 (colour 3), d = 2 → rows 9, 11, …, 21 alternate 2, 3, 2, … ✓"}],"rays":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Extend each seed pixel into a full line perpendicular to the edge it touches"}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"cd505d41d62789a5cec6cd274240895eae24891e25212dd1eeb36ec8494eaf98","task_sha256":"b2db2a51ebf4fa6bcb6ac3f5f16ce6e083452109c7dac7126f81c749dc08c736","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
